        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>The assets of a business are \u20b515,000 and the liabilities are \u20b55,000. What is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity</b>.<br>Rearranged to find owner's equity: <b>Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities</b>.<br>Substitute the given values: \u20b515,000 - \u20b55,000 = <b>\u20b510,000</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
