        "topic": "Bank Reconciliation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>The cash book balance of a business is \u20b512,000 (Dr). The bank statement shows a balance of \u20b510,500. The following items were discovered:<br>- Unpresented cheques: \u20b52,000<br>- Bank charges not recorded: \u20b5500<br>- Deposits in transit: \u20b51,000<br><br>What is the adjusted cash book balance?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>To adjust the cash book balance:<br>1. Start with the cash book balance: \u20b512,000 (Dr).<br>2. Deduct bank charges not recorded: \u20b512,000 - \u20b5500 = <b>\u20b511,500</b>.<br>3. Unpresented cheques and deposits in transit affect the bank statement, not the cash book.</p>",
