    "51739": {
        "order_id": 10,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Incomplete Records",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>A trader's capital at the beginning of the year was \u20b530,000. During the year, he introduced additional capital of \u20b55,000 and withdrew \u20b52,000 for personal use. His capital at the end of the year was \u20b540,000. Calculate the profit or loss for the year.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Profit/Loss = Closing Capital - Opening Capital - Additional Capital + Drawings.<br>Calculation: \u20b540,000 - \u20b530,000 - \u20b55,000 + \u20b52,000 = <b>\u20b57,000 (Profit)</b>.</p>",
